    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0257" n="183" xml:id="pg183"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/799</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-08-30T20:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 2, 12
                        noon.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1684. Petrograd telegram agency prints telegram from Zurich dated 29th that
                    President Wilson will state objects of war by Allies and make last attempt for
                    conciliation and, if fails, markets of the world will be closed to Germany for
                    ten years after war by Allies and America. What foundation?<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d242-f1"/> Such reports harmful in Russia if untrue.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d242-f1" n="1" xml:id="d242-f1-content">
                <p>Answered Sept. 7, No. 1685: “No foundation whatever for report.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
